    "result": "I implemented `compare_versions` in `solution.py` and left the rest of the directory alone. The function parses each version and raises `ValueError` for anything outside the spec: wrong number of core parts, leading zeros in core or numeric prerelease identifiers, empty or non-ASCII identifiers, and malformed build metadata. The `+BUILD` part is validated and then ignored. Precedence is handled by building a comparison key per version: a release with no prerelease sorts above any prerelease with the same core, and prerelease identifiers are compared as tuples where numeric identifiers sort below non-numeric ones and a shorter list sorts lower. The regexes are ASCII-only so Unicode digits are rejected. I did not run anything, since shell access was not available, so the implementation is unverified beyond reading it against the spec.",
